WEBVTT

00:00:03.957 --> 00:00:05.223
Dad. Sam.

00:00:05.257 --> 00:00:06.857
This is bigger than you
think. They're everywhere.

00:00:06.891 --> 00:00:08.824
Sam: if this demon killed mom
and jess and dad's closing in,

00:00:08.857 --> 00:00:10.024
We got to help.

00:00:10.058 --> 00:00:11.590
Dad doesn't want our help.

00:00:11.624 --> 00:00:14.957
I'm talking one week here, man,
to get answers, to get revenge.

00:00:14.991 --> 00:00:16.223
You think i didn't respect dad.

00:00:16.257 --> 00:00:17.891
Sorry i brought it up. I respected him.

00:00:17.924 --> 00:00:19.891
No matter what i did,
it was never good enough.

00:00:19.924 --> 00:00:21.590
So what are you saying? That
dad was disappointed in you?

00:00:21.624 --> 00:00:23.257
When we finally do find dad,

00:00:23.290 --> 00:00:26.091
I don't know if he's
even gonna want to see me.

00:00:26.124 --> 00:00:27.924
Hey! Dad.

00:00:27.957 --> 00:00:29.091
Hey, boys.

00:00:29.124 --> 00:00:31.290
Hi, sam. Hi, dad.

00:00:31.323 --> 00:00:33.924
Last time we were together,
we had one hell of a fight.

00:00:33.957 --> 00:00:36.424
Yes, sir. It's good to see you again.

00:00:36.457 --> 00:00:38.357
It's been a long time.

00:00:38.390 --> 00:00:39.390
Sam!

00:00:39.424 --> 00:00:40.724
Dean: we almost got dad killed.

00:00:40.757 --> 00:00:42.290
They're not gonna stop.
They're gonna try again.

00:00:42.323 --> 00:00:44.024
They're gonna use us to get to him.

00:00:44.058 --> 00:00:45.791
Dad's vulnerable when he's with us.

00:00:45.824 --> 00:00:47.290
I got to be a part of this fight.

00:00:47.323 --> 00:00:48.924
Sammy, this fight is just starting.

00:00:48.957 --> 00:00:51.024
You got to let me go.

00:01:11.357 --> 00:01:12.891
Beth: mr. Elkins?

00:01:15.457 --> 00:01:16.624
Mr. Elkins.

00:01:16.657 --> 00:01:18.724
Would you like another?

00:01:18.757 --> 00:01:21.390
Yeah. Thanks, beth.

00:01:24.323 --> 00:01:26.657
I thought they caught the unabomber.

00:01:26.691 --> 00:01:29.891
Yeah, poor mr. Elkins lives
all alone up in the canyon.

00:01:29.924 --> 00:01:32.657
Same seat every day,

00:01:32.691 --> 00:01:34.957
Going through his papers,
making his little notes.

00:01:34.991 --> 00:01:38.257
He's a nice old man. He's just a nut.

00:01:40.924 --> 00:01:42.457
Here you go.

00:02:08.091 --> 00:02:09.357
What'll you have?

00:02:09.390 --> 00:02:11.824
Jack all around. Leave the bottle.

00:02:11.857 --> 00:02:14.490
You hungry? We have dinner plans.

00:02:18.691 --> 00:02:21.158
Can i get you something
else, mr. Elkins?

00:03:08.857 --> 00:03:10.991
It's been a while.

00:03:11.024 --> 00:03:13.091
I got to say, you look old.

00:03:13.124 --> 00:03:15.424
What do you want? What do you think?

00:03:17.590 --> 00:03:18.924
Damn.

00:03:23.457 --> 00:03:24.724
You can do better than that.

00:03:35.991 --> 00:03:37.524
Come on, come on.

00:04:19.757 --> 00:04:21.091
Nice gun.

00:04:23.190 --> 00:04:25.857
Wouldn't do you much good, of course.

00:04:25.891 --> 00:04:28.390
Boys...

00:04:28.424 --> 00:04:30.824
We're eating in tonight.

00:04:51.091 --> 00:04:53.657
All right, dude, not a decent
lead in all of nebraska.

00:04:53.691 --> 00:04:54.891
What do you got?

00:04:54.924 --> 00:04:57.857
Well, i been scanning wyoming,
colorado, south dakota.

00:04:57.891 --> 00:05:00.991
Here
- A woman in iowa fell 10,000 feet from an airplane

00:05:01.024 --> 00:05:02.757
And survived.

00:05:02.791 --> 00:05:04.557
Sounds more like "that's incredible!"

00:05:04.590 --> 00:05:06.158
Than "the twilight zone."

00:05:06.190 --> 00:05:07.390
Yeah.

00:05:07.424 --> 00:05:10.323
Hey, you know, we could
just keep heading east -

00:05:10.357 --> 00:05:12.557
New york, upstate.

00:05:12.590 --> 00:05:14.924
Could stop by and see sarah again. Huh?

00:05:14.957 --> 00:05:17.524
She's a cool chick, man. Smokin'.

00:05:17.557 --> 00:05:21.058
You two seemed pretty
friendly. What do you say?

00:05:21.091 --> 00:05:23.058
Yeah, i don't know. Maybe someday.

00:05:23.091 --> 00:05:25.824
But in the meantime, we got
a lot of work to do, dean,

00:05:25.857 --> 00:05:27.058
And you know that.

00:05:27.091 --> 00:05:28.757
Yeah, you're right.

00:05:28.791 --> 00:05:30.991
What else you got?

00:05:31.024 --> 00:05:32.257
Uh, man in colorado.

00:05:32.290 --> 00:05:34.624
Local man by the name of daniel elkins

00:05:34.657 --> 00:05:36.524
Was found mauled in his home.

00:05:36.557 --> 00:05:39.091
Elkins. I know that name.

00:05:39.124 --> 00:05:41.091
Doesn't ring a bell.

00:05:41.124 --> 00:05:43.124
Looks like the cops
don't know what to think.

00:05:43.158 --> 00:05:46.490
At first they said it was
some sort of bear attack,

00:05:46.524 --> 00:05:48.824
And now they found signs of robbery.

00:05:48.857 --> 00:05:50.223
Mm-Hmm.

00:05:50.257 --> 00:05:52.424
Yeah.

00:05:55.924 --> 00:05:57.891
Here. Check it out.

00:06:03.724 --> 00:06:05.557
You think it's the same elkins?

00:06:05.590 --> 00:06:07.891
It's a colorado area code.

00:06:45.924 --> 00:06:48.490
Looks like the maid didn't come today.

00:06:54.257 --> 00:06:56.724
Hey, there's salt over
here, right inside the door.

00:06:56.757 --> 00:06:58.991
You mean, like,
protection-Against-Demon salt

00:06:59.024 --> 00:07:00.957
Or "oops, i spilled the popcorn" salt?

00:07:00.991 --> 00:07:02.691
It's clearly a ring.

00:07:07.158 --> 00:07:10.357
You think this guy elkins was a player?

00:07:10.390 --> 00:07:11.457
Definitely.

00:07:20.924 --> 00:07:23.390
That looks a hell of a lot like dad's.

00:07:23.424 --> 00:07:26.857
Except this dates back to the '60s.

00:07:51.791 --> 00:07:54.924
Whatever attacked him, looks
like there was more than one.

00:07:54.957 --> 00:07:57.557
Looks like he put up
a hell of a fight, too.

00:07:57.590 --> 00:07:59.957
Yeah.

00:08:26.357 --> 00:08:28.590
Got something?

00:08:30.257 --> 00:08:33.257
I don't know. Some
scratches in the floor.

00:08:33.290 --> 00:08:34.590
Death throes maybe?

00:08:34.624 --> 00:08:36.457
Maybe.

00:08:55.624 --> 00:08:57.357
Or maybe a message.

00:09:00.124 --> 00:09:03.490
Look familiar?

00:09:03.524 --> 00:09:05.757
Three letters, six digits -

00:09:05.791 --> 00:09:09.791
The location and combination
of a post office box.

00:09:09.824 --> 00:09:11.124
It's a mail drop.

00:09:11.158 --> 00:09:13.091
That's just the way dad does it.

00:09:31.891 --> 00:09:36.024
"J.W."
- You think? John winchester?

00:09:36.058 --> 00:09:38.058
I don't know. Should we open it?

00:09:42.223 --> 00:09:44.058
Dad?

00:09:46.624 --> 00:09:48.924
Dad, what are you doing
here? Are you all right?

00:09:48.957 --> 00:09:49.991
Yeah, i'm okay.

00:09:50.024 --> 00:09:51.524
Look, i read the news about daniel.

00:09:51.557 --> 00:09:54.158
I got here as fast as i could.

00:09:55.924 --> 00:09:58.357
I saw you two up at his place.

00:09:58.390 --> 00:10:00.158
Why didn't you come in, dad?

00:10:00.190 --> 00:10:01.457
You know why.

00:10:01.490 --> 00:10:04.190
Because i had to make sure
you weren't followed...

00:10:04.223 --> 00:10:05.991
By anyone...

00:10:06.024 --> 00:10:07.691
Or anything.

00:10:07.724 --> 00:10:11.058
Nice job of covering
your tracks, by the way.

00:10:11.091 --> 00:10:13.957
Yeah, well, we learned from the best.

00:10:13.991 --> 00:10:16.957
Wait, so you came all the way
out here for this elkins guy?

00:10:16.991 --> 00:10:18.158
Yeah.

00:10:18.190 --> 00:10:22.058
He was
- He was a good man.

00:10:22.091 --> 00:10:24.524
He taught me a hell
of a lot about hunting.

00:10:24.557 --> 00:10:28.024
You never mentioned him to us.

00:10:28.058 --> 00:10:30.590
We had a -

00:10:30.624 --> 00:10:33.257
We had kind of a falling out.

00:10:33.290 --> 00:10:35.924
I hadn't seen him in years.

00:10:37.791 --> 00:10:39.991
I should look at that.

00:10:48.524 --> 00:10:52.590
"If you're reading
this, i'm already dead."

00:10:52.624 --> 00:10:54.891
That son of a bitch. What is it?

00:10:54.924 --> 00:10:57.223
He had it the whole time. Dad, what?

00:10:57.257 --> 00:10:58.757
When you searched the place,

00:10:58.791 --> 00:11:01.190
Did you see a gun, an
antique, a colt revolver?

00:11:01.223 --> 00:11:02.323
Did you see it?

00:11:02.357 --> 00:11:04.557
Uh, there was an old
case, but it was empty.

00:11:04.590 --> 00:11:06.490
They have it. You mean
whatever killed elkins?

00:11:06.524 --> 00:11:08.390
We got to pick up their trail.

00:11:09.924 --> 00:11:12.891
Wait. You want us to come with you?

00:11:12.924 --> 00:11:15.257
If elkins is telling the truth,
we've got to find this gun.

00:11:15.290 --> 00:11:17.757
The gun? Why? Because
it's important, that's why.

00:11:17.791 --> 00:11:20.058
Dad, we don't even know
what these things are yet.

00:11:20.091 --> 00:11:22.091
They were what danny
elkins killed best...

00:11:22.124 --> 00:11:24.257
Vampires.

00:11:24.290 --> 00:11:25.290
Vampires?

00:11:25.323 --> 00:11:27.190
I thought there was no such thing.

00:11:27.223 --> 00:11:29.457
You never even mentioned them, dad.

00:11:29.490 --> 00:11:31.857
I thought they were extinct.

00:11:31.891 --> 00:11:35.924
I thought elkins and
others had wiped them out.

00:11:39.290 --> 00:11:40.657
I was wrong.

00:11:42.657 --> 00:11:46.024
John: most vampire lore is
crap. A cross won't repel them.

00:11:46.058 --> 00:11:47.490
Sunlight won't kill them

00:11:47.524 --> 00:11:49.857
And neither will a stake to the heart.

00:11:49.891 --> 00:11:52.124
But the bloodlust
- That part's true.

00:11:52.158 --> 00:11:54.457
They need fresh human blood to survive.

00:11:54.490 --> 00:11:55.891
They were once people,

00:11:55.924 --> 00:11:59.158
So you won't know it's a
vampire until it's too late.

00:11:59.190 --> 00:12:00.924
All yours, baby.

00:12:07.257 --> 00:12:09.390
What?

00:12:09.424 --> 00:12:11.190
Well, i guess you showed that guy.

00:12:11.223 --> 00:12:13.991
What guy? The guy who bet you
you wouldn't buy that shirt.

00:12:14.024 --> 00:12:16.223
I love this shirt.

00:12:18.891 --> 00:12:20.323
Look out!

00:12:24.691 --> 00:12:26.390
What happened to him?

00:12:26.424 --> 00:12:28.190
Call 911.

00:12:51.954 --> 00:12:54.520
Man: 22, i'm going out there.

00:12:54.554 --> 00:12:56.354
Man #2: copy that.

00:13:01.821 --> 00:13:05.153
Sam, dean, let's go.

00:13:05.187 --> 00:13:06.487
Picked up a police call.

00:13:06.520 --> 00:13:07.687
What happened?

00:13:07.721 --> 00:13:10.187
A couple called 911. They
found a body in the street.

00:13:10.220 --> 00:13:12.021
Cops got there. Everyone was missing.

00:13:12.054 --> 00:13:13.253
It's the vampires.

00:13:13.287 --> 00:13:14.687
How do you know?

00:13:14.721 --> 00:13:16.554
Just follow me, okay?

00:13:18.954 --> 00:13:20.687
Vampires.

00:13:20.721 --> 00:13:23.021
It's funny every time i hear it.

00:13:23.054 --> 00:13:25.220
[ Indistinct chatter on police radio ]

00:13:29.187 --> 00:13:31.587
I don't see why we couldn't
have gone over with him.

00:13:31.621 --> 00:13:33.554
Oh, don't tell me it's already starting.

00:13:33.587 --> 00:13:35.687
What's starting?

00:13:35.721 --> 00:13:37.454
What do you got? It was them all right.

00:13:37.487 --> 00:13:39.088
It looks like they're heading west.

00:13:39.120 --> 00:13:41.220
We have to double back
to get around that detour.

00:13:41.253 --> 00:13:42.621
How can you be so sure?

00:13:42.654 --> 00:13:44.587
I just want to know we're
going in the right direction.

00:13:44.621 --> 00:13:46.253
We are.

00:13:46.287 --> 00:13:48.187
How do you know?

00:13:48.220 --> 00:13:50.253
I found this.

00:13:52.420 --> 00:13:55.554
What is it? A vampire fang?

00:13:55.587 --> 00:13:58.721
No fangs
- Teeth. The second set descends when they attack.

00:13:58.754 --> 00:14:00.420
Any more questions?

00:14:03.654 --> 00:14:05.921
Let's get out of here.
We're losing daylight.

00:14:05.954 --> 00:14:09.721
And, dean, why don't you touch
up your car before you get rust?

00:14:09.754 --> 00:14:11.621
I wouldn't have given you the damn thing

00:14:11.654 --> 00:14:14.253
If i thought you were gonna ruin it.

00:14:21.487 --> 00:14:23.487
Vampires nest in groups of 8 to 10.

00:14:23.520 --> 00:14:25.921
Smaller packs are sent
out to hunt for food.

00:14:25.954 --> 00:14:29.187
Victims are taken to the nest,
where the pack keeps them alive,

00:14:29.220 --> 00:14:31.088
Bleeding them for days or weeks.

00:14:31.120 --> 00:14:33.787
I wonder if that's what
happened to that 911 couple.

00:14:33.821 --> 00:14:35.787
That's probably what dad's thinking.

00:14:35.821 --> 00:14:40.420
Of course, it would be nice if
he just told us what he thinks.

00:14:40.454 --> 00:14:42.287
<i>So it is starting.</i>

00:14:42.320 --> 00:14:45.021
What?

00:14:45.054 --> 00:14:46.921
Sam, we've been looking
for dad all year.

00:14:46.954 --> 00:14:49.287
Now we're not with him for
more than a couple of hours

00:14:49.320 --> 00:14:50.487
And there's static already.

00:14:50.520 --> 00:14:53.253
No.

00:14:53.287 --> 00:14:55.520
Look, i'm happy he's okay, all right,

00:14:55.554 --> 00:14:57.420
And i'm happy that we're
all working together.

00:14:57.454 --> 00:14:59.320
Good.

00:14:59.354 --> 00:15:03.520
It's just the way he treats
us like we're children.

00:15:03.554 --> 00:15:04.988
He barks orders at us, dean.

00:15:05.021 --> 00:15:07.354
He expects us to follow
him without question.

00:15:07.387 --> 00:15:09.687
He keeps us on some
crap need-To-Know deal.

00:15:09.721 --> 00:15:11.654
He does what he does for
a reason. What reason?

00:15:11.687 --> 00:15:12.887
Our job!

00:15:12.921 --> 00:15:14.721
There's no time to argue.
There's no margin for error.

00:15:14.754 --> 00:15:16.220
It's just the way the
old man runs things.

00:15:16.253 --> 00:15:18.120
Yeah, well, maybe that
worked when we were kids,

00:15:18.153 --> 00:15:19.487
But not anymore, all right?

00:15:19.520 --> 00:15:21.721
Not after everything you and
i have been through, dean.

00:15:21.754 --> 00:15:24.187
Are you telling me you're cool
with just falling into line

00:15:24.220 --> 00:15:25.854
And letting him run the whole show?

00:15:27.420 --> 00:15:31.088
If that's what it takes.

00:15:55.220 --> 00:15:57.320
Have some beer, buddy.

00:15:57.354 --> 00:15:59.554
It'll calm your nerves.

00:15:59.587 --> 00:16:01.021
No, thanks.

00:16:01.054 --> 00:16:02.320
Oh, come on.

00:16:02.354 --> 00:16:04.787
You drink enough, i can
taste it in your blood.

00:16:04.821 --> 00:16:06.520
That's gross.

00:16:14.320 --> 00:16:16.021
Well, how about you, babe?

00:16:24.287 --> 00:16:25.520
Attagirl.

00:16:32.153 --> 00:16:34.387
Bo! Wait for luther.

00:16:56.487 --> 00:16:59.220
I missed you, too, baby.

00:16:59.253 --> 00:17:01.854
We've got presents.

00:17:08.287 --> 00:17:09.721
She looks interesting.

00:17:11.787 --> 00:17:12.787
Hmm.

00:17:15.420 --> 00:17:16.654
He doesn't.

00:17:16.687 --> 00:17:18.021
Lock him up.

00:17:20.887 --> 00:17:23.921
On second thought, go
ahead and treat yourself.

00:17:28.988 --> 00:17:32.487
[ Crying ] no!

00:17:32.520 --> 00:17:34.054
There's something else.

00:17:36.021 --> 00:17:37.454
This all theirs?

00:17:37.487 --> 00:17:40.854
No. It's from an old friend of yours...

00:17:40.887 --> 00:17:42.387
Daniel elkins.

00:17:42.420 --> 00:17:44.354
I caught his scent.

00:17:44.387 --> 00:17:46.887
I thought i'd surprise you.

00:17:46.921 --> 00:17:48.787
Kate, what did you do?

00:17:48.821 --> 00:17:50.520
I made him suffer.

00:17:50.554 --> 00:17:52.621
You shouldn't have done that.

00:17:52.654 --> 00:17:54.021
There are others like him.

00:17:54.054 --> 00:17:56.054
They'll know the signs
and come looking for us.

00:17:56.088 --> 00:17:57.153
We have to be careful.

00:17:57.187 --> 00:17:58.454
Luther, i did it for you,

00:17:58.487 --> 00:17:59.988
For what he did to your family.

00:18:00.021 --> 00:18:02.021
Revenge isn't worth
much if you end up dead.

00:18:05.220 --> 00:18:06.887
I'm sorry, babe.

00:18:06.921 --> 00:18:09.253
I'm sorry.

00:18:15.153 --> 00:18:17.153
I thought you might like that.

00:18:17.187 --> 00:18:19.921
Looks like it was made
around the time you were born.

00:18:21.954 --> 00:18:23.821
I've seen this before.

00:18:23.854 --> 00:18:26.387
Elkins died with it in his hands.

00:18:26.420 --> 00:18:30.320
He should have known better
- Using a gun.

00:18:30.354 --> 00:18:33.721
This is no ordinary gun.

00:18:33.754 --> 00:18:35.887
Yeah, dad. All right, got it.

00:18:35.921 --> 00:18:37.988
Pull off the next exit. Why?

00:18:38.021 --> 00:18:40.054
'Cause dad thinks we
got the vampires' trail.

00:18:40.088 --> 00:18:41.120
How?

00:18:41.153 --> 00:18:43.354
I don't know. He didn't say.

00:18:54.854 --> 00:18:57.420
Oh, crap. Here we go.

00:18:57.454 --> 00:18:59.287
What the hell was that? We need to talk.

00:18:59.320 --> 00:19:00.754
About what? About everything.

00:19:00.787 --> 00:19:03.287
Where we going, dad? What's
the big deal about this gun?

00:19:03.320 --> 00:19:05.387
We can q&a after we
kill all the vampires.

00:19:05.420 --> 00:19:07.654
Your brother's right. We
don't have time for this.

00:19:07.687 --> 00:19:10.054
Last we saw you, you said it
was too dangerous to be together.

00:19:10.088 --> 00:19:11.687
Now, out of the blue, you need our help.

00:19:11.721 --> 00:19:14.120
Obviously something big's going
down, and we want to know what!

00:19:14.153 --> 00:19:16.253
Get back in the car. No.

00:19:16.287 --> 00:19:18.520
I said get back in the damn car.

00:19:18.554 --> 00:19:19.921
Yeah, and i said no.

00:19:19.954 --> 00:19:21.621
All right, you made
your point, tough guy.

00:19:21.654 --> 00:19:23.887
Look, we're all tired. We
can talk about this later.

00:19:23.921 --> 00:19:25.187
Sammy, i mean it. Come on.

00:19:25.220 --> 00:19:26.854
This is why i left in the first place.

00:19:26.887 --> 00:19:28.754
What'd you say? You heard me.

00:19:28.787 --> 00:19:29.821
<i>Yeah, you left.</i>

00:19:29.854 --> 00:19:32.287
Your brother and me
- We needed you.

00:19:32.320 --> 00:19:34.854
You walked away, sam. You walked away!

00:19:34.887 --> 00:19:37.320
You're the one who said,
"don't come back," dad.

00:19:37.354 --> 00:19:39.621
You're the one who
closed that door, not me!

00:19:39.654 --> 00:19:42.420
You were just pissed off you
couldn't control me anymore!

00:19:42.454 --> 00:19:44.153
Stop it! Stop it! Stop it!

00:19:44.187 --> 00:19:46.187
That's enough!

00:19:47.687 --> 00:19:49.287
That means you, too.

00:19:57.120 --> 00:19:58.687
Terrific.

00:20:21.954 --> 00:20:24.021
Luther: you like to watch, huh?

00:20:24.054 --> 00:20:26.220
Me too.

00:20:28.487 --> 00:20:30.153
Ready, baby?

00:20:44.520 --> 00:20:47.721
Are you gonna kill me?

00:20:47.754 --> 00:20:52.187
I'm gonna take you so high
you're never gonna come down.

00:21:30.120 --> 00:21:32.487
Welcome home, baby.

00:21:49.827 --> 00:21:51.427
I know what time it is.

00:21:51.460 --> 00:21:52.927
Get in.

00:21:56.261 --> 00:21:59.328
Dean: son of a bitch.

00:21:59.360 --> 00:22:01.827
So they're really not afraid of the sun?

00:22:01.861 --> 00:22:04.694
No, direct sunlight hurts
like a nasty sunburn.

00:22:04.727 --> 00:22:08.594
The only way to kill
them is by beheading.

00:22:08.627 --> 00:22:12.061
And, yeah, they sleep during the day.

00:22:12.094 --> 00:22:15.493
It doesn't mean they won't wake up.

00:22:15.527 --> 00:22:18.994
So i guess walking right
in's not our best option.

00:22:19.027 --> 00:22:21.894
Actually, that's the plan.

00:22:29.927 --> 00:22:31.527
Dad, i've got an extra
machete if you need one.

00:22:31.560 --> 00:22:35.061
Think i'm okay. Thanks.

00:22:35.094 --> 00:22:37.027
Wow.

00:22:43.694 --> 00:22:46.460
So...

00:22:46.493 --> 00:22:49.161
You boys really want
to know about this colt?

00:22:53.261 --> 00:22:54.794
Yes, sir.

00:22:54.827 --> 00:22:57.261
It's just a story...

00:22:57.294 --> 00:23:00.261
A legend, really.

00:23:00.294 --> 00:23:02.393
Well, i thought it was.

00:23:02.427 --> 00:23:05.393
Never really believed it
until i read daniel's letter.

00:23:05.427 --> 00:23:09.294
Back in 1835, when
halley's comet was overhead,

00:23:09.328 --> 00:23:12.927
The same night those
men died at the alamo,

00:23:12.961 --> 00:23:15.861
They say samuel colt made a gun...

00:23:15.894 --> 00:23:17.161
A special gun.

00:23:17.194 --> 00:23:19.261
He made it for a hunter -

00:23:19.294 --> 00:23:22.660
A man like us, only on horseback.

00:23:22.694 --> 00:23:25.627
The story goes he made 13 bullets.

00:23:25.660 --> 00:23:29.594
This hunter used the
gun a half dozen times

00:23:29.627 --> 00:23:33.927
Before he disappeared,
the gun along with him.

00:23:33.961 --> 00:23:37.427
Somehow, daniel got his hands on it.

00:23:37.460 --> 00:23:39.760
They say -

00:23:39.794 --> 00:23:42.427
They say this gun can kill anything.

00:23:42.460 --> 00:23:45.894
Kill anything, like
supernatural anything?

00:23:47.127 --> 00:23:48.894
Like the demon.

00:23:48.927 --> 00:23:50.760
Yeah, the demon.

00:23:50.794 --> 00:23:53.660
Ever since i picked up its trail,

00:23:53.694 --> 00:23:57.861
I've been looking for a
way to destroy that thing.

00:23:57.894 --> 00:24:01.794
Find the gun...

00:24:01.827 --> 00:24:04.328
We may have it.

00:25:35.994 --> 00:25:37.927
Sam: dean.

00:26:01.861 --> 00:26:03.660
There's more.

00:26:38.627 --> 00:26:41.161
Hey.

00:26:41.194 --> 00:26:43.261
Hey, hey, shh. I'm here to help you.

00:26:55.827 --> 00:26:57.493
John: boys, run!

00:26:58.393 --> 00:26:59.594
Dad!

00:27:07.861 --> 00:27:09.427
Dad?!

00:27:11.760 --> 00:27:13.493
Dad?!

00:27:18.727 --> 00:27:21.027
They won't follow. They'll till tonight.

00:27:21.061 --> 00:27:23.460
Once a vampire gets your
scent, it's for life.

00:27:23.493 --> 00:27:24.694
What do we do now?

00:27:24.727 --> 00:27:26.794
You got to find the
nearest funeral home.

00:27:29.560 --> 00:27:31.961
It shouldn't be taking this long.

00:27:31.994 --> 00:27:34.427
I should go help.

00:27:34.460 --> 00:27:36.827
Dean's got it.

00:27:44.360 --> 00:27:46.194
Sammy.

00:27:47.861 --> 00:27:48.861
Yeah?

00:27:51.794 --> 00:27:54.328
I don't think i ever told you this,

00:27:54.360 --> 00:27:57.594
But the day you were
born, you know what i did?

00:27:57.627 --> 00:27:59.694
No.

00:27:59.727 --> 00:28:02.794
I put 100 bucks into a
savings account for you.

00:28:02.827 --> 00:28:05.427
I did the same thing for your brother.

00:28:08.194 --> 00:28:09.727
It was a college fund.

00:28:12.061 --> 00:28:17.228
And every month, i'd put
in another $100 until...

00:28:19.261 --> 00:28:21.660
Anyway, my point is, sam, that

00:28:23.660 --> 00:28:25.794
This is never the life
that i wanted for you.

00:28:25.827 --> 00:28:28.527
Then why'd you get so mad when i left?

00:28:28.560 --> 00:28:32.061
You got to understand something.

00:28:32.094 --> 00:28:34.660
After your mother passed,

00:28:34.694 --> 00:28:38.527
All i saw was evil, everywhere.

00:28:38.560 --> 00:28:44.094
And all i cared about was
keeping you boys alive.

00:28:44.127 --> 00:28:47.594
I wanted you prepared...

00:28:47.627 --> 00:28:49.127
Ready.

00:28:51.360 --> 00:28:53.961
So somewhere along the line, i, uh

00:28:56.660 --> 00:28:58.660
I stopped being your father.

00:28:58.694 --> 00:29:00.560
And i -

00:29:00.594 --> 00:29:04.261
I became your drill sergeant.

00:29:06.294 --> 00:29:10.094
So when you said you
wanted to go away to school,

00:29:10.127 --> 00:29:13.393
All i could think
about, my only thought,

00:29:13.427 --> 00:29:18.460
Was that you were gonna be alone...

00:29:18.493 --> 00:29:20.427
Vulnerable.

00:29:20.460 --> 00:29:23.261
Sammy, it just -

00:29:23.294 --> 00:29:25.427
It never occurred to me what you wanted.

00:29:27.294 --> 00:29:29.594
I just couldn't accept the fact

00:29:29.627 --> 00:29:32.393
That you and me...

00:29:32.427 --> 00:29:33.594
We're just different.

00:29:35.194 --> 00:29:36.460
What?

00:29:39.727 --> 00:29:41.294
We're not different.

00:29:43.727 --> 00:29:45.861
Not anymore.

00:29:48.660 --> 00:29:51.360
With what happened to mom and jess

00:29:55.127 --> 00:29:57.194
We probably have a lot more in common

00:29:57.228 --> 00:29:59.927
Than just about anyone.

00:30:02.294 --> 00:30:04.660
I guess you're right, son.

00:30:08.393 --> 00:30:10.560
Hey, dad?

00:30:12.760 --> 00:30:14.760
Whatever happened to that college fund?

00:30:16.727 --> 00:30:18.527
Spent it on ammo.

00:30:25.594 --> 00:30:26.961
Whoo!

00:30:26.994 --> 00:30:30.493
Man, there's some heavy security
to protect a bunch of dead guys.

00:30:30.527 --> 00:30:32.694
Did you get it?

00:30:42.161 --> 00:30:45.061
You know what to do.

00:30:53.961 --> 00:30:55.627
Kate: car trouble?

00:30:59.794 --> 00:31:01.994
Let me give you a lift...

00:31:02.027 --> 00:31:03.927
Take you back to my place.

00:31:03.961 --> 00:31:05.061
I'll pass.

00:31:05.094 --> 00:31:07.427
I usually draw the line at necrophilia.

00:31:21.727 --> 00:31:25.360
I don't normally get this
friendly till the second date.

00:31:25.393 --> 00:31:28.427
You know, we could have some fun.

00:31:28.460 --> 00:31:31.627
I always like to make new friends.

00:31:41.527 --> 00:31:44.393
Oh, sorry.

00:31:44.427 --> 00:31:46.827
I never really stay
with a chick that long.

00:31:46.861 --> 00:31:48.161
Definitely not eternity.

00:31:48.194 --> 00:31:49.427
Ugh!

00:31:53.861 --> 00:31:55.861
Damn it.

00:31:57.360 --> 00:31:59.194
Barely even stings.

00:31:59.228 --> 00:32:01.560
Give it time, sweetheart.

00:32:01.594 --> 00:32:03.827
That arrow's soaked in dead man's blood.

00:32:03.861 --> 00:32:06.294
It's like poison to you, isn't it?

00:32:09.560 --> 00:32:10.861
Load her up.

00:32:10.894 --> 00:32:13.294
I'll take care of this one.

00:32:23.951 --> 00:32:25.250
Toss this on the fire.

00:32:25.284 --> 00:32:27.384
Saffron, skunks,
cabbage, and trillium -

00:32:27.417 --> 00:32:29.984
It'll block our scent and
hers until we're ready.

00:32:30.018 --> 00:32:31.817
Stuff stinks. Well, that's the idea.

00:32:31.851 --> 00:32:33.517
Dust your clothes with the ashes

00:32:33.551 --> 00:32:35.817
And you'll stand a chance
of not being detected.

00:32:35.851 --> 00:32:37.484
You sure they'll come after her?

00:32:37.517 --> 00:32:39.651
Yeah. Vampires mate for life.

00:32:39.684 --> 00:32:42.150
She means more to the
leader than the gun.

00:32:42.183 --> 00:32:44.117
But the blood sickness
is gonna wear off soon,

00:32:44.150 --> 00:32:45.584
So you don't have a lot of time.

00:32:45.617 --> 00:32:47.083
Half-Hour ought to do it.

00:32:47.117 --> 00:32:49.884
And then i want you out of
the area as fast as you can.

00:32:49.918 --> 00:32:51.117
But -

00:32:51.150 --> 00:32:52.717
You can't take care
of them all yourself.

00:32:52.751 --> 00:32:55.083
I'll have her and the colt.

00:32:55.117 --> 00:32:58.617
But after, we're gonna meet up, right?

00:32:58.651 --> 00:33:02.250
Use the gun together, right?

00:33:04.150 --> 00:33:06.517
You're leaving again, aren't you?

00:33:08.684 --> 00:33:12.150
You still want to go
after the demon alone?

00:33:12.183 --> 00:33:13.651
You know, i don't get you.

00:33:13.684 --> 00:33:16.250
You can't treat us like this. Like what?

00:33:16.284 --> 00:33:17.450
Like children.

00:33:17.484 --> 00:33:20.617
You are my children. I'm
trying to keep you safe.

00:33:20.651 --> 00:33:23.450
Dad, all due respect, but
that's a bunch of crap.

00:33:24.384 --> 00:33:26.517
Excuse me?

00:33:26.551 --> 00:33:28.584
You know what sammy
and i have been hunting.

00:33:28.617 --> 00:33:30.884
Hell, you sent us on a
few hunting trips yourself.

00:33:30.918 --> 00:33:33.050
You can't be that worried
about keeping us safe.

00:33:33.083 --> 00:33:34.617
It's not the same thing, de.

00:33:34.651 --> 00:33:35.751
Then what is it?

00:33:35.784 --> 00:33:37.817
Why do you want us out of the big fight?

00:33:37.851 --> 00:33:39.684
This demon...

00:33:39.717 --> 00:33:42.851
It's a bad son of a bitch.

00:33:42.884 --> 00:33:44.417
I can't make the same moves

00:33:44.450 --> 00:33:46.751
If i'm worried about keeping you alive.

00:33:46.784 --> 00:33:47.951
You can't be as reckless.

00:33:47.984 --> 00:33:49.384
Look...

00:33:49.417 --> 00:33:52.984
I don't expect to make it out
of this fight in one piece.

00:33:55.183 --> 00:33:58.617
Your mother's death...

00:33:58.651 --> 00:34:00.250
It almost killed me.

00:34:01.884 --> 00:34:05.751
I can't watch my children die, too.

00:34:05.784 --> 00:34:06.918
I won't.

00:34:06.951 --> 00:34:08.984
What happens if you die?

00:34:09.018 --> 00:34:10.984
Dad, what happens if you die

00:34:11.018 --> 00:34:13.484
And we could have done
something about it?

00:34:13.517 --> 00:34:14.751
You know, i've been thinking.

00:34:14.784 --> 00:34:16.651
I think maybe sammy's
right about this one.

00:34:16.684 --> 00:34:18.317
I think we should do this together.

00:34:20.584 --> 00:34:23.183
We're stronger as a family,
dad. We just are. You know it.

00:34:24.651 --> 00:34:26.250
We're running out of time.

00:34:27.684 --> 00:34:30.350
You do your job, and
you get out of the area.

00:34:31.584 --> 00:34:33.517
That's an order.

00:34:43.484 --> 00:34:45.684
Is there any sign of those three?

00:34:45.717 --> 00:34:47.651
No. Something else.

00:34:47.684 --> 00:34:49.751
What? Luther, they cut off hank's head.

00:34:49.784 --> 00:34:51.851
And kate?

00:34:51.884 --> 00:34:54.884
I don't know. She wasn't there.

00:34:56.350 --> 00:34:58.018
What are we gonna do?

00:35:03.317 --> 00:35:05.884
It's just a truck up on the highway.

00:35:10.984 --> 00:35:13.417
Kate.

00:35:13.450 --> 00:35:15.717
She's in that truck.

00:36:15.851 --> 00:36:17.284
Boo.

00:36:33.450 --> 00:36:35.684
I told you i'd come back.

00:36:54.450 --> 00:36:56.551
Luther: get out!

00:37:00.784 --> 00:37:02.018
Who are you?

00:37:02.050 --> 00:37:03.384
The name's winchester.

00:37:03.417 --> 00:37:04.851
Where are your friends?

00:37:04.884 --> 00:37:06.450
Cleaning out your nest.

00:37:08.784 --> 00:37:10.484
Where's kate?

00:37:10.517 --> 00:37:12.651
Come here, sweetheart.

00:37:20.250 --> 00:37:22.183
Kate, you all right?

00:37:24.083 --> 00:37:26.317
Dead man's blood.

00:37:26.350 --> 00:37:28.384
You son of a bitch.

00:37:28.417 --> 00:37:32.083
I want the colt
- Elkins' gun.

00:37:32.117 --> 00:37:33.117
Trade.

00:37:33.150 --> 00:37:34.517
Is that what this is all about?

00:37:34.551 --> 00:37:36.350
I mean, you can't shoot us all, right?

00:37:36.384 --> 00:37:37.817
We'll kill you.

00:37:37.851 --> 00:37:40.484
Oh, i don't need it for you.

00:37:40.517 --> 00:37:43.484
I'm saving it for something else.

00:37:43.517 --> 00:37:47.083
Now, put the colt
down or she goes first.

00:37:47.117 --> 00:37:49.717
All right.

00:37:49.751 --> 00:37:52.018
Just don't hurt her.

00:37:59.350 --> 00:38:00.617
Back up.

00:38:02.784 --> 00:38:04.150
Further.

00:38:16.050 --> 00:38:18.551
That's a nice move. You almost made it.

00:38:43.150 --> 00:38:44.183
Ugh!

00:38:48.651 --> 00:38:51.150
Don't! I'll break his neck.

00:38:51.183 --> 00:38:52.851
Put the blade down.

00:39:06.117 --> 00:39:08.717
You people.

00:39:08.751 --> 00:39:10.751
Why can't you just leave us alone?

00:39:10.784 --> 00:39:13.083
We have as much right to live as you do.

00:39:13.117 --> 00:39:14.651
John: i don't think so.

00:39:41.217 --> 00:39:43.884
Luther!

00:39:59.018 --> 00:40:01.117
Kate, don't!

00:40:24.984 --> 00:40:26.984
So, boys...

00:40:31.283 --> 00:40:32.951
Yes, sir?

00:40:32.984 --> 00:40:35.517
You ignored a direct order back there.

00:40:35.550 --> 00:40:37.917
Yes, sir. But we saved your ass.

00:40:43.218 --> 00:40:44.617
You're right.

00:40:44.650 --> 00:40:46.951
I am?

00:40:46.984 --> 00:40:49.350
It scares the hell out of me.

00:40:49.383 --> 00:40:51.250
You two are all i've got.

00:40:53.151 --> 00:40:56.884
But i guess we are stronger as a family.

00:40:56.917 --> 00:40:59.584
So...

00:40:59.617 --> 00:41:03.283
We go after this damn thing...

00:41:03.317 --> 00:41:05.250
Together.

00:41:05.283 --> 00:41:07.517
Yes, sir.Yes, sir.



00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:04.000
